Hi Whitney,

I think this error cropped up with the shift to R 4.3+, where R now objects when a logical test in an if statement is applied to a vector -- here is.na <http://is.na>() is returning multiple results since the EFA list has many outputs (one per number of factors). Anyhow, I believe this was fixed a few days ago in the development version of the package, which you can install using: devtools::install_github("michaelhallquist/MplusAutomation"). I plan to roll out this and some other fixed to CRAN in September.

Best,
Michael

